<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">28 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 28 May, from 585 BCE to 1998.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/lydia" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lydia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">585 BCE <span class="tih-ago">1,441 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Solar eclipse halts a battle between Lydia and Media</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a>, day turned to night during a battle on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kizilirmak">Halys</a> river, and the armies made peace. Astronomers date the eclipse to 28 May 585 BCE, one of the earliest precisely dated events.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lydia">Lydia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1830">1830 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">196 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Andrew Jackson signs the Indian Removal Act</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The law authorised the president to exchange lands west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> for Native territory in the East. It led to the forced removals known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trail-of-tears">Trail of Tears</a>, in which thousands died.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1871">1871 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">155 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Paris Commune falls after the 'Bloody Week'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The last Communard defenders were overcome around the Père Lachaise cemetery. Government troops killed thousands during the week, and the Commune became a lasting symbol for the left.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1918">1918 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Azerbaijan and Armenia declare independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">As the short-lived Transcaucasian federation broke up, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> Democratic Republic and the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> proclaimed independence. Both were absorbed by Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in 1920.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1940">1940 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">King Leopold III surrenders the Belgian army</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After eighteen days of fighting, Leopold III capitulated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> against his government's wishes. The surrender exposed the Allied flank as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dunkirk">Dunkirk</a> evacuation gathered pace.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1998">1998 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">28 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pakistan carries out nuclear tests in Balochistan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> detonated nuclear devices in the Chagai Hills, responding to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>'s tests earlier that month. Both countries now stood as declared nuclear powers.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a></div></div></li></ol>
